description:
Load lesson 4.02's text level format and auto-tile it:

```cpp
struct Point { int x, y; };
struct LevelData
{
    int width{ 0 }, height{ 0 };
    std::vector<std::string> grid;           // only '#', '=' and '.' are left in it
    Point player{ -1, -1 };
    std::vector<Point> enemies, coins;
};

bool loadLevel(const std::string& text, LevelData& out, std::string& error);
int wallMask(const LevelData& level, int x, int y);   // 4-bit auto-tile number, -1 for a non-wall
```

**The format**, one item per line (`\r\n` endings allowed):
- Lines starting with `#` followed by a space, and empty lines, are comments, but **only before** the grid.
- `size W H` (both 1 to 500) must come before the grid. Other header lines (such as `legend ...`) are ignored.
- Then exactly `H` lines of exactly `W` characters. `#` and `=` are walls, `.` is empty, `P` is the player start (exactly one), `E` an enemy and `C` a coin; those letters become `.` in the grid. Any other character is an error.

Errors return `false` with one of these messages: `"missing size"`, `"bad size"`, `"wrong row count"`, `"row N has the wrong length"` (N counting from 1), `"unknown tile 'X' in row N"`, `"no player start"`, `"more than one player start"`.

**wallMask**: for a wall cell, bit 0 is set if the cell above is a wall, bit 1 right, bit 2 below, bit 3 left. Cells outside the map are not walls.

